{\leq} \ & \left(\frac{1}{\alpha}+L+L\sigma_2\right)\|y_+(z)-y\|,
\end{align*}
where the third inequality follows from the $L$-Lipschitz continuity  of $\nabla_y F(\cdot,\cdot)$ and  \eqref{lip-y};  the last inequality follows from the relative error condition of the projected gradient ascent method. This, together with \eqref{OS-GS-better-key3-main}, yields
\[
\|x_r(y(z),z)-x_r(y_+(z),z)\|\leq \frac{\sqrt{2}}{\sqrt{r-L}}\left(\frac{1+\alpha L(1+\sigma_2)}{\alpha\mu}\right)^{\frac{1}{2\theta}} 
\|y-y_+(z)\|^{\frac{1}{2\theta}}.
\]
 \end{enumerate}
The proof is complete.
